          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/thick+subcategory"} thick subcategory
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi KK
                    %mi boot
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi KK
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  KK_{boot} \hookrightarrow KK
          %p
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/triangulated+category"} triangulated category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi KK
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} KK
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KK-theory"} KK-theory
            generated by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+unit"} tensor unit
            is called the
            %em bootstrap category
            (
            %a{:href => "#RosenbergSchochet87"}> Rosenberg-Schochet 87
            ), because on this subcategory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KK-theory"} KK-theory
            has a good
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axiom"} axiomatic
            description (see
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Blackadar"} Blackadar 22.3
          %p
            The canonical
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
            from
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KK-theory"} KK
            to (the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+category"} homotopy category
            of)
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KU"} KU
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/module+spectra"} module spectra
            restricts to a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+and+faithful+functor"} full and faithful functor
            on the bootstrap category (prop.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#StrongMonoidalFullInclusionIntoKUMod"}
            below), and so the KK-bootstrap category may also be thought of as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subcategory"} full subcategory
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi KU
                  %mi Mod
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} KU Mod
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi KK
                    %mi boot
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi Ho
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi KU
                  %mi Mod
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  KK_{boot} \hookrightarrow Ho(KU Mod)
                  \\,.
          %p
            Many
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/C%2A-algebras"} C*-algebras
            that “appear in practice” are in the bootstrap category, notably the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoid+convolution+algebras"} groupoid convolution algebras
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/amenable+Lie+groupoids"} amenable Lie groupoids
            (prop.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ConvolutionOfAmenableLieGroupoid"}
            below). Generally, a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/C%2A-algebra"} C*-algebra
            is in the bootstrap category precisely if it is KK-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence"} equivalent
            to a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+C%2A-algebra"} commutative C*-algebra
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            See (
            %a{:href => "#Blackadar"}> Blackadar, def. 22.3.4
            ).
          %h2#examples_of_objects_in_the_bootstrap_category Examples of objects in the bootstrap category
          #ConvolutionOfAmenableLieGroupoid.num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoid+convolution+algebra"} groupoid convolution algebra
              of an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/amenable+topological+groupoid"} amenable topological groupoid
              is in the bootstrap category.
          %p
            This is due to (
            %a{:href => "#Tu99"}> Tu 99, prop. 10.7
            ), recalled for instance as (
            %a{:href => "#Uuye11"}> Uuye 11, example 3.6
            ).
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#knneth_theorem Künneth theorem
          %p
            In the bootstrap category a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K%C3%BCnneth+theorem"} Künneth theorem
            for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/operator+K-theory"} operator K-theory
            is true. (
            %a{:href => "RosenbergSchochet87"}> Rosenberg-Schochet 87
            ).
          %h3#embedding_into_module_spectra
            Embedding into
            = succeed "-module" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi KU
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} KU
          #StrongMonoidalFullInclusionIntoKUMod.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              On the bootstrap category the operator K-theory spectrum functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi KK
                    %mo →
                    %mi Ho
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi KU
                    %mi Mod
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} KK \to Ho(KU Mod)
              is
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  a
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fully+faithful+functor"} fully faithful functor
              %li
                %p
                  a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strong+monoidal+functor"} strong monoidal functor
          %p
            The first statement is (
            %a{:href => "DEKM11"}> DEKM 11, section 3
            ), the second is (
            %a{:href => "#DEKM11"}> DEKM 11, prop. 4.2
            ).
          %p
            See at
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KK-theory"} KK-theory
            the section
            %em
              %a{:href => "KK-theory#TriangulatedAndSpectrumEnrichedStructure"} Triangulated and spectrum-enriched structure
            for more details.
          %h2#references References
          %p The notion originates in
          %ul#RosenbergSchochet87
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jonathan+Rosenberg"}> Jonathan Rosenberg
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Claude+Schochet"} Claude Schochet
              = succeed "," do
                %em The Künneth theorem and the universal coefficient theorem for Kasparov’s generalized K-functor
          %p A texbook account is around def. 22.3.4 of
          %ul#Blackadar
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bruce+Blackadar"}> Bruce Blackadar
              ,
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K-Theory+for+Operator+Algebras"} K-Theory for Operator Algebras
          %p
            The corresponding
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/localizing+subcategories"} localizing subcategories
            are discussed in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ivo+Dell%27Ambrogio"}> Ivo Dell'Ambrogio
              ,
              %em
                Localizing subcategories in the Bootstrap category of separable C
                %em
                  \-algebras_, Journal of K-Theory 8 (2011), 493-50 (
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1003.0183"}> arXiv:1003.0183
                  )
          %p The full embedding into the homotopy category of KU-modules is discussed in section 3 of
          %ul#DEKM11
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ivo+Dell%27Ambrogio"}> Ivo Dell'Ambrogio
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Heath+Emerson"} Heath Emerson
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tamaz+Kandelaki"} Tamaz Kandelaki
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ralf+Meyer"} Ralf Meyer
              %em A functorial equivariant K-theory spectrum and an equivariant Lefschetz formula
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1104.3441"}> arXiv:1104.3441
              )
          %p
            The inclusion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoid+convolution+algebras"} groupoid convolution algebras
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/amenable+topological+groupoids"} amenable topological groupoids
            into the bootstrap category is discussed in
          %ul#Tu99
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jean-Louis+Tu"}> Jean-Louis Tu
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em La conjecture de Baum-Connes pour les feuilletages moyennables
          %ul#Uuye11
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Otgonbayar+Uuye"}> Otgonbayar Uuye
              ,
              %em
                A note on the Künneth theorem for nonnuclear
                = succeed "-algebras" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi C
                          %mo *
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\ast
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1111.7228"}> arXiv:1111.7228
              )
          %p
            Discussion of the bootstrap category in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+K-theory"} equivariant K-theory
            is in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Heath+Emerson"}> Heath Emerson
              ,
              %em Localization techniques in circle-equivariant KK-theory
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1004.2970"}> arXiv:1004.2970
              )
          %p
            This show that there are algebras in the plain bootstrap category with
            = succeed "-equivariant" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle+group"} circle group
            = succeed "-equivariant" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U(1)
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U(1)
            = succeed "-alegbra." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\ast
